<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Version>1.3.0</Version>
    <PackageId>TokenGuard.Core</PackageId>
    <Title>TokenGuard.Core</Title>
    <Authors>Svetlozar Stoykov</Authors>
    <Company>Svetlozar Stoykov</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Svetlozar Stoykov</Copyright>
    <Description>Token budget management for .NET 10 LLM agent loops. Tracks conversation growth, masks stale tool output, summarizes older history when needed, and keeps requests within a configured limit. Targets net10.0 only.</Description>
    <PackageTags>tokenguard;llm;ai;agents;context-management;token-budget;prompt-management;openai;anthropic;dotnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Opens the library to custom parts: the public ILlmSummarizer contract with replaceable summary instructions, WithTokenCounter for one counter shared across contexts, WithCompactionStrategy for a custom strategy per conversation, and a public EstimatedTokenCounter. Prepare results report stage counts, the unchanged prefix, the summarization status and a token breakdown, also as tags on tokenguard.prepare activities. SlidingWindowOptions.ExemptToolNames names tools whose results are never masked.

Behavior changes, with no signature changes: a recorded tool result above a token limit, on by default at the smaller of 25,000 and a quarter of MaxTokens, is stored shortened with a notice in place of its middle; the compaction strategy receives its budget on the estimate scale, inverted from the provider correction; pretty-printed JSON is charged for its whitespace; a tool result is masked only when its placeholder is smaller; the summarizer request is built to a token budget and its output cap is twice the target; summarizer diagnostics name the summarizer type and normalize finish reasons. Prepared views can differ from those of 1.2.0 for the same history. Fixes text holding half of a surrogate pair, a provider input count of zero, and an invalid placeholder format.

Known limits: one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas until the first provider report; with the tool result limit turned off, one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.

Full details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.Tests" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TokenGuard.IntegrationTests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
